# ============================================================
# Zolo Packing frontend — environment template
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local      (development)
#   cp .env.example .env.production (production build)
#
# SECURITY: every VITE_* value is INLINED INTO THE PUBLIC BROWSER BUNDLE at
# build time. Anyone can read them with View Source.
#
# NEVER put DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, BANK_ENC_KEY, an admin password, or any
# other server secret in this file. Those belong in server/.env (development)
# or the platform's environment variables (production), and are read only by
# the API process — never shipped to a browser.
#
# This project uses exactly ONE frontend variable, and it is OPTIONAL. If you
# are deploying the standard single-service setup, this file can stay empty:
# no .env is required to build the frontend.
# ============================================================

# Base URL of the Zolo API. OPTIONAL — see src/lib/api-config.ts.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET in both development and the recommended production setup:
#
#   development  -> falls back to http://localhost:5001/api/v1
#   production   -> falls back to same-origin "/api/v1", which the Node
#                   process serves directly (see server.mjs), or which nginx
#                   proxies to the API container (see nginx.conf)
#
# Same-origin is preferable because the browser makes no cross-origin requests
# at all, so CORS never applies and there is nothing to misconfigure.
#
# Only set this when the API is on a DIFFERENT host to the frontend. If you do,
# that frontend origin must ALSO be listed in the API's CORS_ORIGINS or every
# request will be refused with 403:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://api.zolopackaging.com/api/v1"
